+A follow-up round (2026-07-09 through 2026-07-10) evaluated three further
+candidates under the identical protocol. \textbf{MiLMMT-46-4B}
+(\texttt{xiaomi-research/MiLMMT-46-4B-v0.1}, the same Gemma3-based causal-LM
+family as the deployed 1B model, 4-bit bitsandbytes NF4) scored 68.5 BLEU /
+81.8 chrF at 34\,chars/s --- the highest quality of any model evaluated in
+this project, exceeding even Seamless-medium's float16 67.0 BLEU. Its VRAM
+peak of 8{,}050\,MiB (98.8\% of the 8\,GB card) is too tight to make the
+default; it is deployed opt-in only, with MiLMMT-46-1B remaining the
+default. Qualitative verification on a real 90-paragraph Bengali story found
+no hallucination, an exact paragraph-count match, and correction of
+mistranslations present in the 1B model's output. This is the inverse of
+the Hunyuan-MT-7B result above: there, 4-bit quantization of a 7B model
+lost to full-precision smaller models; here, 4-bit quantization of a 4B
+model beats a float16 2.3B specialist. Quantization loss is therefore
+architecture- and training-data dependent, not a fixed penalty
+predictable from parameter count alone.
+
+Two further candidates were rejected despite acceptable FLORES-200 scores,
+illustrating that benchmark BLEU does not predict real-document
+reliability. Sarvam AI's \textbf{sarvam-translate}
+(\texttt{sarvamai/sarvam-translate}, a Gemma3-4B fine-tune by Sarvam AI
+with AI4Bharat, positioned as the de-facto IndicTrans3 successor) scored
+55.7 BLEU / 74.3 chrF at 4{,}880\,MiB VRAM, but degenerated into a
+repetition loop on the same real story --- 62\% of output paragraphs
+repeated filler text rather than translating the source. Ola Krutrim's
+\textbf{krutrim-translate} (\texttt{krutrim-ai-labs/Krutrim-Translate}, a
+CTranslate2 float16 distillation of IndicTrans2) scored 44.9 BLEU / 73.1
+chrF at 1{,}608\,MiB VRAM --- below even NLLB-600M --- and its internal
+\texttt{ben\_Beng eng\_Latn} control tag leaked into approximately 41\% of
+output paragraphs on the real-story evaluation. Both are rejected; every
+model in this round that passed the FLORES-200 bar was subsequently
+verified against a real story before an accept/reject call.
+
